---
import GuideLayout from "../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro";
import LearningGuideGrid from "../../components/LearningGuideGrid.astro";
import {learningGuides} from "../../learningGuides";
const referenceGuides = [
    ["Scene Settings", "Sky color, gravity, music, and scene-level events.", "fpe-scene-settings", "scene-settings"],
    ["Characters, Players and Cameras", "Player rigs, NPCs, cameras, and control styles.", "fpe-characters-players-and-cameras", "characters"],
    ["Animation and Frame Events", "Imported animation, timed events, and playback control.", "fpe-animation-and-events", "animation"],
    ["Audio", "Speakers, ambience, looping, and background music.", "fpe-audio", "audio"],
    ["Triggers and Commands", "Trigger filters, scene events, and the command catalog.", "fpe-triggers-commands", "triggers"],
    ["Inventory and Holdables", "Item kinds, quantities, slots, and physical held objects.", "fpe-inventory-and-holdables", "inventory"],
    ["Conversations", "Dialogue resources, replies, progression, and events.", "fpe-conversations", "conversations"],
    ["UI and Cursors", "Menus, overlays, UI elements, and pointer behavior.", "fpe-ui", "ui-elements"],
    ["Input", "Default actions, controllers, and runtime remapping.", "fpe-input", "input"],
    ["Cameras", "Player cameras, fixed views, switching, and cutscenes.", "fpe-cameras", "cameras"],
    ["Sub-scenes and Level Loading", "Interiors, streamed regions, fades, and full level changes.", "fpe-subscenes-and-levels", "sub-scene"],
    ["Troubleshooting", "Export, import, runtime, trigger, and level-flow checks.", "fpe-troubleshooting", "troubleshooting"],
    ["Physics and Colliders", "Rigid bodies, collider generation, and movement settings.", "fpe-physics-and-colliders", "physics"],
    ["Pipeline and Runtime", "GLB import, feature registration, loading, and cleanup.", "fpe-pipeline", "pipeline"],
];
---
<GuideLayout title="Godot Game Development Guides" description="Practical guides to Godot inventory, triggers, interactive objects, animation events, dialogue, holdable items, and Blender level workflows." hideGuideIndexBreadcrumb={true}>
    <Fragment slot="head"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/learning-guides.css"/></Fragment>
    <section class="web-splash"><div class="web-splash-inner base-background"><img class="web-splash-img" src="/assets/images/guide-splash.png" alt="Folded Paper Engine guide owl"></div></section>
    <section class="section top-section"><header><img class="title-graphic" src="/assets/images/guide-icon.png" alt=""><div class="section-title">Game Development Guides<div class="section-subtitle">Solve the Godot problem first. Use FPE when it makes the work faster.</div></div></header><div class="section-body"><p>Each guide starts with a real game-development problem and a clear Godot 4 solution. The final section shows how Folded Paper Engine can move repeated setup into the Blender scene without hiding the underlying Godot concepts. Use either workflow—or combine them.</p><LearningGuideGrid guides={learningGuides}/></div></section>
    <section class="section"><header><div class="section-title">Folded Paper Engine Reference<div class="section-subtitle">Exact settings, commands, and runtime behavior</div></div></header><div class="section-body"><p>Already using FPE and need the precise feature documentation? These references contain the complete authoring and runtime details behind the problem-first guides.</p><div class="doc-grid">{referenceGuides.map(([title, description, slug, image]) => <a class="doc-card" href={`/docs/${slug}.html`}><span class="doc-card-title" style={`background-image:url('/docs/thumbs/${image}.png')`}>{title}</span><span class="doc-card-body">{description}</span></a>)}</div></div></section>
</GuideLayout>
